Below is a cohesive, step-by-step guide followed by copy-paste-ready TypeScript/TSX code for each file. It covers MarkdownRX integration, a multi-page docs system (App Router), Tailwind-styled editor, Firebase (Firestore + Storage), client boundaries with "use client", and formatting guidance.

Step-by-step instructions

1) Install dependencies
- Core
  - npm i firebase
- Markdown pipeline
  - npm i unified remark-parse remark-gfm remark-slug remark-rehype rehype-sanitize hast-util-sanitize rehype-autolink-headings rehype-highlight rehype-stringify
- Optional (recommended for preview readability)
  - npm i -D @tailwindcss/typography
  - Add the plugin in tailwind.config.js and use className="prose" on preview containers.

2) Environment and Firebase setup
- Add a .env.local with:
  - NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=...
  - NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=...
  - NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=...
  - NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=...
  - NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=...
  - NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=...
- Ensure you have a Firestore database and Storage bucket.
- Security rules: set appropriate auth/permissions as needed for your app.

3) Firestore schema
- Collection: docs
- Doc ID: slug (string, URL-friendly)
- Fields:
  - title: string
  - content: string (markdown)
  - tags?: string[]
  - createdAt: Firestore Timestamp (serverTimestamp on create)
  - updatedAt: Firestore Timestamp (serverTimestamp on update)

4) Client vs Server components and "use client"
- Any component using React state/effects, Firebase client SDK, onSnapshot, or DOM APIs must include "use client" at the top.
- Server components can fetch initial data server-side (if needed), but here we subscribe client-side for live updates.
- Pages under app/docs and app/docs/[slug] will render client components for interactive features.

5) Formatting guidance for docs
- Use consistent heading hierarchy (#, ##, ###).
- Fenced code blocks (```lang) for snippet clarity; highlight.js will colorize.
- Tables and GFM lists are supported via remark-gfm.
- Links and images are sanitized; only safe attributes are allowed by the extended sanitize schema.
- Optional frontmatter is not parsed here; keep metadata in Firestore fields (title, tags).
- Raw HTML in markdown is disallowed for safety (rehype-sanitize + disallow raw HTML in remark-rehype).

